  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>K</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> represent electric field and propagation vectors of the EM waves in vacuum, then magnetic field vector is given by:</p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>-</mo></math> angular frequency)</p>"
